# GitLab Pages redirect rules, copied to the root of public/ by the `pages`
# job. See .gitlab/ci/docs.yml.
#
# The book is served from /xquad/, so the host root would otherwise be a dead
# end. Send it to the main Quip documentation, which as of QUI-1272 is served
# from developers.quip.network/docs rather than quip.gitbook.io/docs.
# Domain-level (external) redirects are generally available since GitLab 17.4
# and accept only 301/302.
#
# The documentation's six top-level groups are listed individually rather than
# covered by a catch-all. A /* rule would also claim /xquad/toolchain, which
# this host correctly 404s but the docs host serves as a different document
# inside the book's own prefix. It would also leave public/404.html
# unreachable for every path, because ServeNotFoundHTTP runs only after both
# tryFile and tryRedirects miss.
#
# QUI-1331 moves the book to developers.quip.network/docs/xquad/. Once that
# lands this host holds no content of its own, and these rules collapse to a
# single catch-all.
/                          https://developers.quip.network/docs                               301
/getting-started/*         https://developers.quip.network/docs/getting-started/:splat         301
/quip-interlock-protocol/* https://developers.quip.network/docs/quip-interlock-protocol/:splat 301
/compute/*                 https://developers.quip.network/docs/compute/:splat                 301
/basics/*                  https://developers.quip.network/docs/basics/:splat                  301
/network/*                 https://developers.quip.network/docs/network/:splat                 301
/nodes/*                   https://developers.quip.network/docs/nodes/:splat                   301
